<Project>
    <ItemGroup Condition="'$(IsPackable)' == 'true'">
        <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)fantomas_logo.png" Visible="false" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
        <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)README.md" Visible="false" Pack="true" PackagePath="" />
        <PackageReference Include="Ionide.KeepAChangelog.Tasks" PrivateAssets="all" />
        <PackageReference Include="DotNet.ReproducibleBuilds" PrivateAssets="all" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <!--
      Overrides the CallFsYacc target from the FsLexYacc package. This file is imported after the
      package's targets, so this definition is the one that runs.

      fsyacc prints every shift/reduce and reduce/reduce conflict it finds, unconditionally: there
      is no quiet or nowarn flag. For pars.fsy that is over 1400 lines of conflict reports on every
      run. We vendor the grammar files verbatim from dotnet/fsharp, pinned by FCSCommitHash, and
      never author or change them, so the reports say nothing we can act on and only bury the rest
      of the build log. StandardOutputImportance="low" hides them at normal verbosity while leaving
      them available at -v:detailed. The trade is that a genuinely regressed grammar arriving with
      an FCSCommitHash bump surfaces as a compile error rather than a conflict report.
      Reported upstream as fsprojects/FsLexYacc#241.

      The target is copied rather than wrapped because the package's version has two bugs:

        1. Outputs lists only %(Filename).fs and omits the .fsi, so a missing or stale .fsi on its
           own does not trigger a regeneration. dotnet/fsharp's own copy of this target in
           buildtools/buildtools.targets lists both. See fsprojects/FsLexYacc#231.
        2. The FileWrites ItemGroup is a copy-paste of the one in CallFsLex and registers the fslex
           output paths, so the generated parsers are never removed by dotnet clean.

      Once those are fixed and released, this override can go away.
    -->
    <Target Name="CallFsYacc"
            Inputs="@(FsYacc)"
            Outputs="@(FsYacc->'$(FsYaccOutputFolder)%(Filename).fs');@(FsYacc->'$(FsYaccOutputFolder)%(Filename).fsi')"
            Condition="'@(FsYacc)'!=''"
            BeforeTargets="CoreCompile">
        <MakeDir Directories="$(FsYaccOutputFolder)" />
        <Exec Command="$(FsLexYaccToolRunner)&quot;$(FsYaccToolPath)\$(FsYaccToolExe)&quot; -o &quot;$(FsYaccOutputFolder)%(FsYacc.Filename).fs&quot; %(FsYacc.OtherFlags) %(FsYacc.Identity)"
              StandardOutputImportance="low" />
        <ItemGroup>
            <FileWrites Include="$(FsYaccOutputFolder)%(FsYacc.Filename).fs;$(FsYaccOutputFolder)%(FsYacc.Filename).fsi" />
        </ItemGroup>
    </Target>
</Project>
